            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-13033",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "nodemailer: Nodemailer: Email to an unintended domain can occur due to Interpretation Conflict"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A vulnerability was identified in the email parsing library due to improper handling of specially formatted recipient email addresses. An attacker can exploit this flaw by crafting a recipient address that embeds an external address within quotes. This causes the application to misdirect the email to the attacker's external address instead of the intended internal recipient. This could lead to a significant data leak of sensitive information and allow an attacker to bypass security filters and access controls."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-13033",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-13033\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: nodemailer\nFixed Version: 7.0.7\nLink: [CVE-2025-13033](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-13033)\nA vulnerability was identified in the email parsing library due to improper handling of specially formatted recipient email addresses. An attacker can exploit this flaw by crafting a recipient address that embeds an external address within quotes. This causes the application to misdirect the email to the attacker's external address instead of the intended internal recipient. This could lead to a significant data leak of sensitive information and allow an attacker to bypass security filters and access controls.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-13033**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|nodemailer|7.0.7|[CVE-2025-13033](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-13033)|\n\nA vulnerability was identified in the email parsing library due to improper handling of specially formatted recipient email addresses. An attacker can exploit this flaw by crafting a recipient address that embeds an external address within quotes. This causes the application to misdirect the email to the attacker's external address instead of the intended internal recipient. This could lead to a significant data leak of sensitive information and allow an attacker to bypass security filters and access controls."
              },
